{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-7923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,F=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,G=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-7923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $D$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(D)=3\\cdot 6-6\\cdot 2=6.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(D)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $D$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $F$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(F)=6\\cdot 6-6\\cdot 6=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(F)=0,$ we conclude that $F$ is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $G$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(G)=(-2)\\cdot 4-4\\cdot 2=-16.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(G)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $G$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $F$ does not have an inverse." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-7923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b8a338119d773f18183b964e1d0ec6c948d1b5ea5ebaaac0f518e848bed090ec"} {"question" "q-7923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-7923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$D$ and $F$ only"] ["text" "$D$ and $G$ only"] ["text" "$F$ and $G$ only"] ["text" "$F$ only"] ["text" "$G$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-7923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$F$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-11726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $P=[\\begin{aligned}n & -8 \\\\ -2 & n\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $n.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-11726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $P$ is singular if and only if $det(P)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =n\\cdot n-(-2)\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & ={n}^{2}-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ {n}^{2} & =16 \\\\ n & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $n$ are $n=\\pm 4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-11726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b8a338119d773f18183b964e1d0ec6c948d1b5ea5ebaaac0f518e848bed090ec"} {"question" "q-11726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-11726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "n=-2"] ["math" "n=-4"] ["math" "n=4"] ["math" "n=\\pm 2"] ["math" "n=\\pm 4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-11726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "n=\\pm 4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=-2\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot 6=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(A)=0,$ we conclude that $A$ is not invertible. Since $A$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $A$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 5-7\\cdot 0=5.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b8a338119d773f18183b964e1d0ec6c948d1b5ea5ebaaac0f518e848bed090ec"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$  and $C$ only"] ["text" "$A$ only"] ["text" "$B$  and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ only"] ["text" "$C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-127821" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$A$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-127901" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}48 & a \\\\ a & 3\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $a.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-127901" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =48\\cdot 3-a\\cdot a \\\\  & =144-{a}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}144-{a}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2} & =144 \\\\ a & =\\pm 12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $a$ are $a=\\pm 12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-127901" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b8a338119d773f18183b964e1d0ec6c948d1b5ea5ebaaac0f518e848bed090ec"} {"question" "q-127901" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-127901" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a=1"] ["math" "a=2"] ["math" "a=\\pm 12"] ["math" "a=\\pm 4"] ["math" "a=\\pm 9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-127901" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a=\\pm 12"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-275738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}x-5 & x+3 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-275738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(x-5)\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot (x+3) \\\\  & =-3x+15-2x-6 \\\\  & =-5x+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5x+9 & =0 \\\\ -5x & =-9 \\\\ x & =\\frac{9}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-275738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b8a338119d773f18183b964e1d0ec6c948d1b5ea5ebaaac0f518e848bed090ec"} {"question" "q-275738" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"} {"question" "q-275738" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991694/state.json" "file_sha256" "007e293b2cdb635a007484941a2b74cfe7444cd35e6110f06d5ac00601e3ceb9"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1032 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
